{"title":"Selva Ceramics","sub":"A busy tile factory with collapsing margins","type":"Profitability","industry":"Building materials","geo":"Spain","diff":2,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Complexity cost · changeovers · cost to serve","prompt":"Selva Ceramics makes porcelain floor and wall tiles in Castellón, Spain. It sold a record 8.4 million m² this year (8.0M the year before) and the factory has never been busier, yet operating profit fell from $5.2M to $1.26M. The CEO asks you to find out why.","clarify":[{"q":"Prices?","a":"Flat at about $7.00 per m² at the factory gate."},{"q":"Energy prices?","a":"The gas price Selva pays fell slightly last year."},{"q":"What has changed commercially?","a":"Selva started accepting small custom orders from architects and designers: special colours and sizes."},{"q":"Objective?","a":"Restore profit to at least $4M without losing the design customers."}],"structure":{"root":"Why did profit fall when volume grew?","branches":[{"head":"Revenue","items":["Price per m²","Volume","Mix: standard vs custom"]},{"head":"Variable cost per m²","items":["Materials","Kiln energy","Packaging","Line labour"]},{"head":"Fixed costs","items":["Plant, maintenance, overheads"]}]},"hypothesis":"Price is flat and volume is up, so cost per m² must have risen. With gas prices falling, I'd look at how much energy each m² uses, which depends on how the kilns are run.","questions":[{"q":"Here is cost per m² by component. Where did profit go?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"396.533pt\" height=\"191.004pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 396.533 191.004\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 191.004 L 396.533 191.004 L 396.533 -0 L 0 -0 L 0 191.004 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 43.373 165